15
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.140
I'm working out some head congestion.

16
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.240
She's got a little bit of a stuffy nose.

17
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:53.760
I know.

18
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.360
Can you hear it?

19
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.460
I feel like you can hear it.

20
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.940
Lee said you can hear it.

21
00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.580
He said I should acknowledge it when I got on air.

22
00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.820
I can hear it.

23
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.340
It doesn't bother me, lady.

24
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.620
Well, he said just right off the bat, if you just acknowledge it, then you know it's fine.

25
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.040
It's like when I had food poisoning.

26
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.940
I was like, hey, we're talking to Ellie.

27
00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.300
I also sound like I just crawled out of the bathroom.

28
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:16.760
Exactly.

29
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.000
Yeah.

30
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.900
Okay, so there we go.

31
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:20.820
It's been said.

32
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.040
Now moving on to Whistleblower.

33
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:23.560
Yeah.

34
00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.460
This episode, which was written by Warren Lieberstein and Halstead Sullivan and directed

35
00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.200
