41
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.460
Lady, I have to say, I hadn't watched this episode since it aired.

42
00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:52.980
Mm-hmm.

43
00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:53.300
Same.

44
00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.060
And I really enjoyed it.

45
00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:55.720
I did too.

46
00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.460
There's so many great moments.

47
00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.960
Well, there's a lot of Kathy Bates in this episode, and that made me very happy.

48
00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.680
There's a lot of Joe and Michael, which I could not get enough of.

49
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.260
Same.

50
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.600
I mean, they're two amazing actors doing amazing work.

51
00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:10.940
Yeah.

52
00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.140
All right.

53
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.160
Fast fact number one, like we said, this is the season six finale.

54
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.280
It aired on May 20th,

55
00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.500
2010, and was watched by 6.6 million households.

56
00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.600
Now, if I remember correctly, Angela, we were

57
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:32.640
originally only going to do 24 episodes, and at the last minute, suddenly we were doing 26.

58
00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.380
This was confirmed by our writers, Warren and Halstead.

59
00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.100
Yes, because we reached out to them for this episode, and they shared with us lots of fun

60
00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.860
behind-the-scenes stuff that we'll share and sprinkle through the episode.

61
00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:50.660
Well, Warren and Halstead did share with us that the finale had this dual purpose of both

62
00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:55.360
having to wrap up season six as well as set things up for season seven.

63
00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.280
You know, in past years,

64
00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.540
our season finales have had some pretty big cliffhangers, and this one has a few,

65
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.700
but they're maybe not as dramatic as other years.

66
00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.800
Right, but you know what's interesting about that to me?

67
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.420
If you have been watching all along,

68
00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.640
which we have now, right?

69
00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.400
We're watching every week.

70
00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.400
Just when Michael mentions Holly,

71
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.460
that felt so huge to me.

72
00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:17.160
Yes.

73
00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:24.880
Okay, so I remember that at this time, we knew that Steve would only be coming back for season

74
00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.180
seven, and that was it.

75
00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:31.680
By the time we did this episode, it was, we found out kind of a few episodes

76
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.120
before the end of season six, so the writers knew that that season seven would be his last,

77
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.500
and Warren and Halstead shared that they had started brainstorming what Steve's last year

78
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:48.760
might look like, and the big thing that they settled on was that they wanted him to ultimately

79
00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:55.220
find happiness with Holly, and that was going to be a seed that was planted in this season finale.

80
00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:59.100
But besides that, they only set up two other things.

81
00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.320
They set up that Dwight was going to buy

82
00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.840
the building, and we start to see Erin kind of warming up to Andy.

83
00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:11.040
She touches his calf, kind of, and lets her hand linger there for a minute.

84
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.280
It is a lingering calf touch.

85
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:13.900
Touch, yeah.

86
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.480
For sure.

87
00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:14.880
Uh-huh.

88
00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.240
Lingering calf touch.

89
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:22.460
Well, like you said, Warren and Halstead were awesome, and we've got some fun little tidbits

90
00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.560
from them for this episode.

91
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.220
Thank you, guys.

92
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:24.680
Yeah.

93
00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.300
Are you ready for fast fact number two?

94
00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.180
I'm so ready.

95
00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.760
Please tell me it's a location breakdown.

96
00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.420
Of a private plane?

97
00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:32.840
Yes.

98
00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.240
It sure is, lady.

99
00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:42.420
We shot that private plane on location at the Van Nuys Airport on board an actual private plane

100
00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.040
that was not a set.

101
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.260
We got some fan mail.

102
00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:49.080
People wondered if we built the interior of a fakie plane.

103
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.200
No, that was a real plane, and it was very narrow, and our camera operators, that was a bit of a

104
00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.140
challenge to figure out how to shoot, because they couldn't move any seats.

105
00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.060
They couldn't move any

106
00:04:59.060 --> 00:04:59.480
walls.

107
00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:00.900
They were just crammed in there.

108
00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.060
Our production designer, Michael Gallenberg,

109
00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:11.500
was friends with a senior executive at the aviation company called Castle & Cook,

110
00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.840
and because of that, we were able to use their hanger and the interior of their jet

111
00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.460
for a cost of only $10,000.

112
00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:25.380
Plus, we had to pay the Van Nuys Airport Authority a $5,000 usage fee.

113
00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.320
Oh, the usage fees.

114
00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:28.100
You know those.

115
00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.480
The dang usage fees.

116
00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:38.520
So, Castle & Cook is a real aviation company, and it only exists in Van Nuys, California,

117
00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.160
and Honolulu, Hawaii.

118
00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.900
So, you are not going to ever find this anywhere near Scranton, Pennsylvania.

119
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:52.080
But Warren and Halstead shared that they were writing this script up to the very last minute,

120
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.500
and by the time they got the idea to shoot on a private plane, they did not have time to change

121
00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.340
the Castle & Cook signage to something else.

122
00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.140
They couldn't make, like, a giant new hanger sign.

123
00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:04.580
Yeah.

124
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.180
So, they just went with it.

125
00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:12.600
Incidentally, Castle & Cook is part of the company that

126
00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.380
originally owned Dole Fruit.

127
00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:15.580
What?

128
00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:16.260
Yeah.

129
00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.480
They are one of the largest suppliers of Hawaiian pineapples.

130
00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.440
Well, I guess they fly them on their planes.

131
00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:22.440
I guess.

132
00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.100
Well, who knows?

133
00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:24.660
Who knows?

134
00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:30.140
I would hope that if I'm on a Castle & Cook private plane, someone serves me some fresh Hawaiian pineapple.

135
00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.580
And if they don't, you'll bring it up.

136
00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.360
I sure will.

137
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:33.820
I'll be like,

138
00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:37.240
you guys, you don't even have any canned pineapple back there?

139
00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:37.960
It's your thing.

140
00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.940
Well, listen, they didn't have time to change the big sign, but there are some really great details

141
00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:46.620
