00:54:50.620 --> 00:54:56.080
It basically links up all of your communication portals, and he does a demonstration.

1277
00:54:56.080 --> 00:55:02.960
Where he sends himself a Wolf, which then gives him a notification on all of his devices at once.

1278
00:55:03.180 --> 00:55:06.040
Even Aaron notifies him via intercom.

1279
00:55:06.220 --> 00:55:07.400
He gets a fax.

1280
00:55:07.620 --> 00:55:08.840
It pops up on his screen.

1281
00:55:09.100 --> 00:55:09.280
His phone.

1282
00:55:09.440 --> 00:55:09.960
Like, everything.

1283
00:55:10.100 --> 00:55:11.180
All goes off at once.

1284
00:55:11.180 --> 00:55:12.020
Everything goes off.

1285
00:55:12.400 --> 00:55:17.540
Well, a lot of people wrote in to say this was the first mention of Wolf, and it is.

1286
00:55:17.980 --> 00:55:22.200
Warren and Halstead said that this just started as a one-off joke for this episode.

1287
00:55:22.200 --> 00:55:24.380
They kind of came up with it in the writer's room.

1288
00:55:24.520 --> 00:55:28.320
But it is eventually going to become a whole episode in season seven.

1289
00:55:28.800 --> 00:55:29.100
Yes.

1290
00:55:29.260 --> 00:55:35.280
I reached out to writer Aaron Schur, because I know he writes the episode Wolf eventually, right?

1291
00:55:35.500 --> 00:55:40.920
And he said he pitched the name Wolf, but someone else pitched the idea of it.

1292
00:55:41.060 --> 00:55:46.500
But how he came up with the name was he said Twitter was just starting, and he thought the

1293
00:55:46.500 --> 00:55:49.880
sound a dog makes instead of a bird was funny.

1294
00:55:50.160 --> 00:55:50.400
Oh, yeah.

1295
00:55:50.560 --> 00:55:51.140
That's good.

1296
00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:52.520
I like it.

1297
00:55:52.640 --> 00:55:52.800
Yeah.

1298
00:55:53.360 --> 00:55:59.040
Randy shared that they had everything rigged to go off at the same time, but that Ellie does

1299
00:55:59.040 --> 00:56:00.480
not actually call on the phone.

1300
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:06.340
To time that out, they had her just standing off camera to do her line, and then in post-production,

1301
00:56:06.340 --> 00:56:09.880
they put an effect on her voice to make it sound like it was from the phone.

1302
00:56:10.080 --> 00:56:13.320
Well, I have to point out one thing about Ryan in this scene.

1303
00:56:13.320 --> 00:56:17.700
And he has now officially combined all of his new looks.

1304
00:56:18.160 --> 00:56:19.160
Did you catch it?

1305
00:56:19.280 --> 00:56:23.240
It's glasses, suspenders, bow tie, orange watch.

1306
00:56:24.060 --> 00:56:24.540
Wow.

1307
00:56:24.760 --> 00:56:26.360
The only thing missing is his hat.

1308
00:56:26.480 --> 00:56:28.360
It's kind of like he's woofed his wardrobe.

1309
00:56:28.460 --> 00:56:29.900
He's woofed his wardrobe.

1310
00:56:31.140 --> 00:56:35.400
Well, if Michael was freaking out that he had two whistleblowers, now his mind is completely

1311
00:56:35.400 --> 00:56:37.820
blown because he has three whistleblowers.

1312
00:56:38.320 --> 00:56:42.880
His solution to this is that they just smash all the computers, destroy the evidence.

1313
00:56:43.320 --> 00:56:43.660
Yes.

1314
00:56:43.920 --> 00:56:49.160
But really, Pam says, I think you just need to convince Joe to go easy on all of us.

1315
00:56:49.300 --> 00:56:53.300
And then once we know our jobs are safe, we all confess at once.

1316
00:56:53.400 --> 00:56:54.760
So this is going to be the new plan.

1317
00:56:55.980 --> 00:56:58.680
Meanwhile, Toby is in the break room.

1318
00:56:58.900 --> 00:57:01.180
His snack is stuck in the vending machine.

1319
00:57:01.900 --> 00:57:07.380
And he starts doing the thing where you kind of jiggle and try to move the vending machine.

1320
00:57:07.960 --> 00:57:11.720
Dwight offers to help him, but he gets a call in the middle.

1321
00:57:12.160 --> 00:57:16.080
And then Toby's stuck just sort of holding up the vending machine.

1322
00:57:16.920 --> 00:57:18.320
They've tipped it forward.

1323
00:57:18.660 --> 00:57:21.640
When I saw that, I was like, wait, was that in the script?

1324
00:57:21.760 --> 00:57:25.440
It had to have been in the script because it's such a big prop move.

1325
00:57:25.440 --> 00:57:27.860
I couldn't figure out how he was doing it.

1326
00:57:28.400 --> 00:57:35.760
According to thepromove.com, vending machines weigh between 400 and 900 pounds when they are empty.

1327
00:57:35.940 --> 00:57:36.420
Wow.

1328
00:57:36.820 --> 00:57:39.780
And you really can't move them without proper equipment.

1329
00:57:39.780 --> 00:57:42.440
So I asked Randy Cordray about it.

1330
00:57:42.680 --> 00:57:49.880
He said that Mike Thompson, our on-set special effects technician, rigged the back of the machine with a safety cable.

1331
00:57:50.120 --> 00:57:52.760
And it went all the way through that back wall.

1332
00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:56.220
And then Mike Thompson stood behind there.

1333
00:57:56.420 --> 00:58:00.740
He said this was the area, Jenna, where our lunch tables usually were.

1334
00:58:01.340 --> 00:58:05.980
That, I guess, really is only something we can visualize, Angela.

1335
00:58:05.980 --> 00:58:08.000
But just so you know, Mike's standing there.

1336
00:58:08.140 --> 00:58:08.300
Yeah.

1337
00:58:08.440 --> 00:58:10.040
He's got this cord through the wall.

1338
00:58:10.220 --> 00:58:13.960
He had manipulated it so that the machine could tilt at a certain angle.

1339
00:58:14.340 --> 00:58:17.040
But Mike was actually holding the weight.

1340
00:58:17.440 --> 00:58:19.480
And so it could never fall.

1341
00:58:19.720 --> 00:58:21.360
Like, that cable was holding it.

1342
00:58:21.440 --> 00:58:23.340
So it couldn't actually fall on Paul.

1343
00:58:23.500 --> 00:58:25.780
And that's how they did it, very convincingly.

1344
00:58:26.820 --> 00:58:28.560
So Michael's going to go up to Joe.

1345
00:58:28.700 --> 00:58:31.420
And he's going to be like, you know, on second thought about this whistleblower,

1346
00:58:31.520 --> 00:58:33.840
I think we make them work, come in here.

1347
00:58:33.880 --> 00:58:34.940
And they just got to work.

1348
00:58:34.940 --> 00:58:37.080
Yeah, they get to totally keep their job.

1349
00:58:37.460 --> 00:58:40.860
And she's like, Michael Scott, what do you know?

1350
00:58:41.860 --> 00:58:43.200
But he's not going to tell her.

1351
00:58:43.580 --> 00:58:45.680
No, she's going to bring them into the conference room.

1352
00:58:45.680 --> 00:58:47.220
And they just kind of face off.

1353
00:58:47.520 --> 00:58:49.780
He will not tell her what he knows.

1354
00:58:50.380 --> 00:58:53.140
There's a great moment where she says, Michael, speak.

1355
00:58:53.540 --> 00:58:54.060
Speak!

1356
00:58:54.440 --> 00:58:56.600
And then the dog barks on the couch.

1357
00:58:57.300 --> 00:58:59.660
We had a fan question from Enoch N.

1358
00:58:59.820 --> 00:59:00.940
and Sarah M.

1359
00:59:01.080 --> 00:59:02.720
from Pennsylvania and others

1360
00:59:02.720 --> 00:59:08.040
who wanted to know, when Joe says speak and the dog barks, was that scripted or improvised?

1361
00:59:08.920 --> 00:59:11.180
Well, I did not see it in the script.

1362
00:59:11.620 --> 00:59:13.160
I have an answer for you.

1363
00:59:13.280 --> 00:59:13.500
Oh.

1364
00:59:13.820 --> 00:59:18.260
Because Warren and Halstead told me that the dog barking and Joe saying speak

1365
00:59:18.260 --> 00:59:20.600
were something that they came up with on the day.

1366
00:59:20.800 --> 00:59:21.080
Ooh.

1367
00:59:21.080 --> 00:59:26.120
And luckily for us, the dog trainer was able to get the dog to Hal on command.

1368
00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:28.540
Well, I'm glad because that was a good bit.

1369
00:59:28.700 --> 00:59:29.520
I loved it.

1370
00:59:29.720 --> 00:59:34.740
And Randy shared with us that the same Great Danes as before were our dog actors, Gabby

1371
00:59:34.740 --> 00:59:35.320
and Guinness.

1372
00:59:35.480 --> 00:59:36.980
I felt like I recognized them.

1373
00:59:37.360 --> 00:59:37.860
Did you?

1374
00:59:37.960 --> 00:59:38.320
I did.

1375
00:59:38.440 --> 00:59:39.460
I knew they were the same.

1376
00:59:39.620 --> 00:59:41.720
You could kick Gabby and Guinness out of a Great Danes crowd?

1377
00:59:41.720 --> 00:59:45.420
I don't know which one is which, but when they walked in the door at the very beginning,

1378
00:59:45.600 --> 00:59:46.800
I thought, same Danes.

1379
00:59:47.520 --> 00:59:48.400
Same Danes.

1380
00:59:48.700 --> 00:59:54.640
Well, at the end of this meeting, Joe is going to invite Michael to leave with her.

1381
00:59:55.980 --> 00:59:59.280
And she drives him to a small airport.

1382
00:59:59.620 --> 01:00:01.660
I love how paranoid Michael is.

1383
01:00:01.700 --> 01:00:04.060
He's like, I've got a dinner with chief of police.

1384
01:00:04.180 --> 01:00:05.540
Like, what does he think Joe's up to?

1385
01:00:05.700 --> 01:00:06.080
I know.

1386
01:00:06.080 --> 01:00:06.940
Like, just in case.

1387
01:00:07.260 --> 01:00:08.860
She's like up to something shady.

1388
01:00:08.940 --> 01:00:11.220
He has some plans to meet with officials.

1389
01:00:12.120 --> 01:00:16.560
Meanwhile, Dwight is getting ready to wrap up his real estate deal because he's buying

1390
01:00:16.560 --> 01:00:18.320
that property that Joe suggested.

1391
01:00:19.000 --> 01:00:22.480
But he sees a sign while he's on the phone with his realtor.

1392
01:00:22.600 --> 01:00:24.180
It says Scranton Business Park.

1393
01:00:24.620 --> 01:00:25.820
He has an idea.

1394
01:00:26.280 --> 01:00:28.120
Make him an offer they can't refuse.

1395
01:00:28.260 --> 01:00:29.200
Actually lowball them.

1396
01:00:29.360 --> 01:00:30.000
Just get it done.

1397
01:00:30.280 --> 01:00:30.560
Yeah.

1398
01:00:30.880 --> 01:00:32.880
He's going to buy the building.

1399
01:00:33.540 --> 01:00:36.220
We had a fan question from Ashley S.

1400
01:00:36.460 --> 01:00:37.220
in the UK.

1401
01:00:37.860 --> 01:00:40.800
When Dwight makes an offer on the Scranton Business Park,

1402
01:00:41.920 --> 01:00:43.320
1725 Slough Avenue,

1403
01:00:43.620 --> 01:00:45.700
was that a nod to the British show,

1404
01:00:45.840 --> 01:00:47.300
which was set in Slough?

1405
01:00:47.780 --> 01:00:48.560
Yes, it was.

1406
01:00:48.600 --> 01:00:49.120
Of course it was.

1407
01:00:49.260 --> 01:00:50.040
Yes, it was.

1408
01:00:50.180 --> 01:00:51.780
That has always been our address.

1409
01:00:52.020 --> 01:00:54.860
It's even on Michael Scott's business card from the pilot.

1410
01:00:55.080 --> 01:00:55.280
Yeah.

1411
01:00:55.660 --> 01:00:57.180
Which you and I both took one.

1412
01:00:57.300 --> 01:00:58.200
Of course we did.

1413
01:00:58.360 --> 01:00:58.800
Of course we did.

1414
01:00:58.920 --> 01:00:59.140
Yes.

1415
01:00:59.700 --> 01:01:02.820
Randy shared that that big business park sign in the background

1416
01:01:02.820 --> 01:01:03.980
that says Dunder Mifflin,

1417
01:01:04.120 --> 01:01:06.560
that was put up just for that scene,

1418
01:01:06.560 --> 01:01:08.060
and then it was quickly taken down.

1419
01:01:08.060 --> 01:01:10.640
He said we never wanted to draw attention to ourselves.

1420
01:01:10.640 --> 01:01:14.380
We did not want to have a sign that said Dunder Mifflin

1421
01:01:14.380 --> 01:01:15.540
out on the street like that.

1422
01:01:15.780 --> 01:01:15.900
Right.

1423
01:01:16.740 --> 01:01:17.820
Back in the bullpen,

1424
01:01:18.120 --> 01:01:20.100
Gabe has concluded his investigation.

1425
01:01:20.860 --> 01:01:21.320
Yes.

1426
01:01:21.560 --> 01:01:24.000
He says Andy did it based on all the evidence.

1427
01:01:24.140 --> 01:01:25.380
And everyone agrees.

1428
01:01:25.800 --> 01:01:28.180
Although Jim does try to make Andy feel better,

1429
01:01:28.260 --> 01:01:29.780
but then Andy just throws him under the bus.

1430
01:01:29.920 --> 01:01:30.660
By the way,

1431
01:01:30.900 --> 01:01:32.780
Gabe didn't do a very good job investigating

1432
01:01:32.780 --> 01:01:35.440
because David Wallace pops in for a talking head

1433
01:01:35.440 --> 01:01:37.920
where he says that he did it.

1434
01:01:38.580 --> 01:01:39.440
He's like,

1435
01:01:39.600 --> 01:01:41.820
he heard from an old client about their problems,

1436
01:01:41.820 --> 01:01:44.360
and he immediately started spreading the news.

1437
01:01:45.320 --> 01:01:46.940
But he's not really here to talk about that.

1438
01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:47.820
He wants to talk about Socket.

1439
01:01:47.940 --> 01:01:49.560
He only wants to talk about Socket.

1440
01:01:49.960 --> 01:01:51.360
Speaking of that talking head,

1441
01:01:51.480 --> 01:01:51.660
Ange,

1442
01:01:51.760 --> 01:01:53.680
we had a fan catch from Sarah H.

1443
01:01:53.760 --> 01:01:55.000
in Williamsburg, Virginia,

1444
01:01:55.020 --> 01:01:55.720
who said,

1445
01:01:55.820 --> 01:01:57.100
as a dog-obsessed person,

1446
01:01:57.100 --> 01:02:00.200
I always get excited whenever we visit David Wallace's house

1447
01:02:00.200 --> 01:02:01.600
because he has a dog.

1448
01:02:02.060 --> 01:02:04.320
But in David's talking head,

1449
01:02:04.440 --> 01:02:06.220
this is not the same dog as before.

1450
01:02:07.100 --> 01:02:09.220
David originally had a golden retriever,

1451
01:02:09.220 --> 01:02:11.760
and now it looks like he has a hound mix

1452
01:02:11.760 --> 01:02:13.300
or a pointer of some kind.

1453
01:02:14.220 --> 01:02:15.020
Sarah says,

1454
01:02:15.260 --> 01:02:17.020
this is not a groundbreaking discovery,

1455
01:02:17.020 --> 01:02:18.420
but I thought it was kind of fun

1456
01:02:18.420 --> 01:02:20.040
that the Wallace has got a new dog.

1457
01:02:20.440 --> 01:02:22.360
Well, I have an answer for you, Sarah.

1458
01:02:22.700 --> 01:02:24.420
I thought I recognized this dog

1459
01:02:24.420 --> 01:02:25.440
when I watched the episode,

1460
01:02:25.640 --> 01:02:26.640
and I reached out to Warren,

1461
01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:27.860
and he confirmed it.

1462
01:02:28.220 --> 01:02:30.140
This was Paul Lieberstein's dog.

1463
01:02:30.140 --> 01:02:31.580
His name was Dude.

1464
01:02:31.980 --> 01:02:34.500
Wait, this is Paul's dog in real life?

1465
01:02:34.520 --> 01:02:36.620
Yes, it's Paul's dog in real life.

1466
01:02:36.700 --> 01:02:37.600
His name was Dude.

1467
01:02:37.840 --> 01:02:39.800
He was the sweetest dog.

1468
01:02:40.080 --> 01:02:41.320
I love that dog.

1469
01:02:41.760 --> 01:02:42.980
Oh, my gosh.

1470
01:02:43.280 --> 01:02:44.580
He was like one of those big dogs

1471
01:02:44.580 --> 01:02:45.840
who thinks he's a lap dog.

1472
01:02:46.080 --> 01:02:47.040
This is so funny

1473
01:02:47.040 --> 01:02:49.320
because I wrote to Randy about this question,

1474
01:02:49.320 --> 01:02:50.460
and I said,

1475
01:02:51.240 --> 01:02:52.540
what is this dog?

1476
01:02:52.720 --> 01:02:54.260
Was this Bob Dunn's?

1477
01:02:54.260 --> 01:02:54.520
Yeah.

1478
01:02:54.840 --> 01:02:57.400
Animal menagerie dog?

1479
01:02:57.400 --> 01:02:58.100
No.

1480
01:02:58.560 --> 01:02:58.660
No.

1481
01:02:58.660 --> 01:02:59.300
And he said,

1482
01:02:59.540 --> 01:03:01.840
Jenna, I have no record of this dog.

1483
01:03:01.840 --> 01:03:02.940
I can't believe it.

1484
01:03:02.980 --> 01:03:04.320
I don't know who the dog is.

1485
01:03:04.660 --> 01:03:05.620
It was Dude.

1486
01:03:06.080 --> 01:03:06.520
Wow.

1487
01:03:06.860 --> 01:03:07.920
I love it.

1488
01:03:08.540 --> 01:03:08.920
Well, lady,

1489
01:03:09.020 --> 01:03:10.380
I think we stay in the bullpen

1490
01:03:10.380 --> 01:03:12.960
because Nick is going to have such a big scene.

1491
01:03:13.140 --> 01:03:14.340
Let's let all this play out,

1492
01:03:14.420 --> 01:03:15.720
and then we'll go back to the plane

1493
01:03:15.720 --> 01:03:16.960
where Michael and Joe are.

1494
01:03:17.000 --> 01:03:17.760
I like that.

1495
01:03:18.400 --> 01:03:20.100
Yeah, Nick, the IT guy,

1496
01:03:20.580 --> 01:03:22.340
he's going to say goodbye to everyone

1497
01:03:22.340 --> 01:03:23.720
because he's going to Detroit

1498
01:03:23.720 --> 01:03:25.320
with Teach for America.

1499
01:03:25.320 --> 01:03:26.120
Mm-hmm.

1500
01:03:26.360 --> 01:03:28.600
No one can even remember his name, Jenna.

1501
01:03:28.880 --> 01:03:29.800
I know, and Gabe is like,

1502
01:03:29.900 --> 01:03:30.800
this is not the time.

1503
01:03:30.800 --> 01:03:32.620
I am talking about an investigation.

1504
01:03:33.140 --> 01:03:34.820
I forgot how badly

1505
01:03:34.820 --> 01:03:37.040
the whole bullpen blows off Nick.

1506
01:03:37.380 --> 01:03:38.100
Poor guy.

1507
01:03:38.240 --> 01:03:40.040
He was just trying to say a nice goodbye.

1508
01:03:40.420 --> 01:03:41.020
I know.

1509
01:03:41.580 --> 01:03:42.540
Nick is like,

1510
01:03:42.660 --> 01:03:43.360
you know what?

1511
01:03:43.980 --> 01:03:45.260
I've kind of had it.

1512
01:03:45.680 --> 01:03:47.680
I've looked at all your hard drives,

1513
01:03:47.720 --> 01:03:50.280
and he starts revealing all these truths.

1514
01:03:50.540 --> 01:03:50.880
Yeah.

1515
01:03:50.880 --> 01:03:52.600
And then he says,

1516
01:03:52.840 --> 01:03:54.200
and I'll tell you what,

1517
01:03:55.400 --> 01:03:57.200
Andy is the whistleblower.

1518
01:03:57.380 --> 01:03:58.160
I saw it.

1519
01:03:58.260 --> 01:03:59.600
He wrote a note to the press.

1520
01:03:59.880 --> 01:04:01.400
Then he gives everybody the finger

1521
01:04:01.400 --> 01:04:02.080
and walks out.

1522
01:04:02.180 --> 01:04:03.660
Yeah, he does a two-bird salute

1523
01:04:03.660 --> 01:04:04.700
on the way out.

1524
01:04:05.160 --> 01:04:06.520
We had a fan question

1525
01:04:06.520 --> 01:04:07.320
from Kyle T.

1526
01:04:07.520 --> 01:04:08.420
in Houston, Texas.

1527
01:04:08.860 --> 01:04:10.840
Did Nick call out other people

1528
01:04:10.840 --> 01:04:12.420
that we did not get to see?

1529
01:04:13.200 --> 01:04:14.980
Yes, Kyle, he did.

1530
01:04:15.680 --> 01:04:17.480
He has a dig at Jim and Pam

1531
01:04:17.480 --> 01:04:18.700
that I remember

1532
01:04:18.700 --> 01:04:19.900
from when we were shooting.

1533
01:04:20.140 --> 01:04:21.280
